{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For we have been sold.</b> From the niphal binyan, and the meaning is like אחר מכרנו והנה והתמכרת — that they sell themselves and there is no buyer." "<b>And if.</b> Like ואילו חיה אלף שנים (Ecclesiastes 6:6) [and its parallel], and the alef is added. The meaning: for we have been sold להשמיד (to destroy [us]), and if we had been sold להיותנו עבדים ושפחות (to be male and female slaves), I would have kept silent, for this trouble that has come upon us is not equal in our eyes to anything — even though there is nothing above killing — so that the king not come to harm in his thinking. And behold, הצר is a noun, like צר ומצוק מצאוני (Psalm 119:143). Or הצר is an adjective: for the enemy is not one that harm should come to the king. And the word נזק in Aramaic: לא להוי נזיק."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {1 "The repeated phrase ואילו חיה אלף שנים appears twice in the Hebrew; Ibn Ezra cites Ecclesiastes 6:6 twice, apparently as two attestations of the same construction, or one citation and its parallel verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:14.688339192Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}